WEBVTT

00:31.900 --> 00:33.860
What a drag...

00:39.740 --> 00:42.070
Would you get away from me already?!

01:09.890 --> 01:11.480
It left!

01:22.320 --> 01:24.240
Oh, it's you, Watanuki.

01:24.320 --> 01:27.240
You don't just come up and bang into me,
and then say "Oh, it's you"!

01:27.330 --> 01:30.250
Don't go standing around on the
side of the road. You're in the way.

01:30.330 --> 01:34.670
What?! You've got a lot of nerve, Domeki!

01:34.750 --> 01:37.670
Watanuki-<i>kun</i>, Domeki-<i>kun</i>...

01:37.750 --> 01:40.840
Himawari-<i>chan</i>!

01:40.920 --> 01:43.260
Summer vacation starts tomorrow.

01:43.340 --> 01:46.640
Yeah, but I've got to work
during the whole vacation.

01:46.720 --> 01:49.220
Domeki-<i>kun</i>, do you have anything planned?

01:49.310 --> 01:50.220
Not especially.

01:50.310 --> 01:51.810
What about you, Himawari-<i>chan</i>?

01:51.890 --> 01:55.650
I'm going over to a relative's
house for the <i>Obon</i> festival.

01:55.730 --> 01:59.650
But then, I won't be able to see you all.
I'm going to miss you a little.

01:59.730 --> 02:03.240
Mm-hmm, me too. In any case, I've
got nothing but my hellish job ahead.

02:03.320 --> 02:04.660
I won't miss you.

02:04.740 --> 02:06.240
We weren't talking to you!

02:06.320 --> 02:11.250
Just go on ahead without me! I'm going
to enjoy walking Himawari-<i>chan</i> home!

02:11.330 --> 02:13.830
Well, if you'll excuse me...

02:13.910 --> 02:15.880
Yeah, see you.

02:17.750 --> 02:19.670
You too, Watanuki-<i>kun</i>.

02:19.750 --> 02:22.510
Take care!

02:28.890 --> 02:33.230
My beloved Kunogi Himawari-<i>chan</i>...
My whole school life is because of you.

02:33.310 --> 02:36.810
Usually, summer vacation is something
that students look forward to,

02:36.900 --> 02:39.820
but to me, it is a time of bitter farewells!

02:39.900 --> 02:40.690
Later.

02:40.730 --> 02:42.820
You head on home on your own!

02:42.900 --> 02:44.860
Shoo! Shoo! Shoo!

02:49.740 --> 02:51.660
That spook is coming back!

02:51.740 --> 02:54.250
No matter how much these things
stay away when Domeki is around,

02:54.330 --> 02:57.670
I still don't want to be around him.

02:57.750 --> 03:02.090
So why do these things always have to haunt <i>me</i>?!

03:03.340 --> 03:06.840
For crying out loud, this is a curse,
having a predisposition to seeing,

03:06.930 --> 03:11.100
feeling, and being influenced
by these things, I tell you!

03:15.890 --> 03:18.650
There are many unusual things in this world,

03:18.730 --> 03:22.230
but no matter how peculiar
or bizarre a phenomenon is,

03:22.320 --> 03:27.820
if people are not there, and if people
do not see them, they fade like mirages.

03:27.910 --> 03:31.240
People... people... people...

03:31.330 --> 03:35.870
It is <i>people</i> who are the most
mysterious things in the world.

03:49.340 --> 03:51.640
Why, you--!

03:51.720 --> 04:01.720
Why, you... you... you... you...

04:12.320 --> 04:16.290
So... heavy...

04:23.340 --> 04:25.710
Just a little farther...

05:05.340 --> 05:07.240
Invitation

05:05.750 --> 05:07.300
What's this?

05:14.930 --> 05:17.220
The Master is waiting for you.

05:17.310 --> 05:19.230
Huh? Waiting?

05:19.310 --> 05:20.680
For you.

05:21.890 --> 05:24.270
Yay! He's back!

05:27.730 --> 05:29.690
Welcome back!

05:33.910 --> 05:36.660
Yuko-<i>san</i>?

05:36.740 --> 05:39.250
Watanuki...

05:39.330 --> 05:40.700
Saké.

05:42.330 --> 05:43.870
- Saké.
- Saké.

05:43.960 --> 05:44.710
Saké!

05:44.750 --> 05:48.250
Geez, of all things, saké?!
In the middle of the day?!

05:48.340 --> 05:52.260
I've run out of my favorite Junmai Daiginjo.

05:52.340 --> 05:54.840
It's your own fault for drinking
it all at once, for crying out loud.

05:54.930 --> 05:57.810
There aren't any liquor stores
that have this in stock anymore.

05:57.890 --> 05:59.810
I'll go place an order for you, though.

05:59.890 --> 06:02.640
So, Ichihara Yuko-<i>san</i>, my employer,

06:02.730 --> 06:05.230
cleaning, laundry, gardening, or cooking,

06:05.310 --> 06:06.810
what would you like me to start with today?

06:06.900 --> 06:07.820
All of them.

06:07.900 --> 06:09.230
All of them?!

06:09.320 --> 06:11.820
Don't yell in my ears.

06:11.900 --> 06:17.830
I've been granting your wish to
keep the spooks from seeing you,

06:17.910 --> 06:21.870
and to keep the spooks
from haunting you, haven't I?

06:23.330 --> 06:26.880
In exchange, you are providing

06:26.960 --> 06:30.250
a commensurate amount
of manual labor for me.

06:30.340 --> 06:33.260
Okay then, today I'll let you get off with

06:33.340 --> 06:35.840
just sorting out my treasure storeroom.

06:35.930 --> 06:39.220
Ah, for the love of... Oh, yeah...

06:39.310 --> 06:40.680
Here.

06:42.890 --> 06:46.650
Judging by the text of this, it looks
more like I'm being called out than invited.

06:46.730 --> 06:47.860
What does it say?

06:48.900 --> 06:50.270
Would you like to know?

06:52.900 --> 06:56.860
Nope. Once you've told me, you're just going
to demand more compensation from me, right?

07:07.330 --> 07:10.670
Sheesh, how much of this is there?!

07:10.750 --> 07:11.670
Lots.

07:11.750 --> 07:13.260
- Lots.
- Lots.

07:13.340 --> 07:16.840
Geez! If you've got this much, you
could have some of it taken somewhere!

07:16.930 --> 07:21.640
I can't have that. This is all here to
be handed down to someone, after all.

07:21.720 --> 07:25.640
I didn't mean to collect it all, but it
got collected anyhow, so what can I do?

07:25.730 --> 07:29.650
That's what everyone who
can't straighten up says.

07:29.730 --> 07:30.860
What's this?

07:32.320 --> 07:34.230
That tickles!

07:34.320 --> 07:37.820
You're Watanuki. It's spelled like
"April 1st," but pronounced "Watanuki."

07:37.910 --> 07:40.660
Don't go hiding in her treasures!

07:40.740 --> 07:43.910
Hey! Get off! I can't breathe! I can't breathe!

07:53.920 --> 07:55.300
I've found you.

07:56.760 --> 07:59.840
The one who can help me.

07:59.930 --> 08:03.890
Um... you must be here to see Yuko-<i>san</i>.

08:16.320 --> 08:17.240
Was there something...

08:17.320 --> 08:18.820
No...

08:18.900 --> 08:20.860
Can I...

08:21.910 --> 08:25.240
...really have any wish
I want granted here?

08:25.330 --> 08:27.250
Yes, by Yuko-<i>san</i>.

08:27.330 --> 08:31.880
Whatever wish you may have,
I can grant it for you.

08:34.340 --> 08:38.840
However, I will also have to take a
commensurate amount of compensation.

08:38.920 --> 08:41.680
There she goes, just like I did,
getting caught in the trap,

08:41.760 --> 08:43.850
and falling prey to Yuko-<i>san</i>'s poisonous fangs.

08:43.930 --> 08:45.810
- A poisonous bite!
- A poisonous bite!

08:45.890 --> 08:46.850
You there!

08:48.890 --> 08:52.230
I will pay you any compensation you want.

08:52.310 --> 08:56.650
Thank goodness. When I first heard
about you, I couldn't believe it.

08:56.730 --> 08:59.650
How could there be a shop that
grants any wish you wanted?

08:59.740 --> 09:03.820
A fortune teller that I know happened
to introduce me to this place.

09:03.910 --> 09:09.250
There are no happenstances in this world.
The only thing there is is inevitability.

09:09.330 --> 09:11.830
It was inevitable that you would come here.

09:11.920 --> 09:16.670
That means that it is inevitable
that I will grant you your wish.

09:16.750 --> 09:20.670
Let's hear... what your wish is.

09:20.760 --> 09:23.260
I need you to help me.

09:23.340 --> 09:27.810
I can no longer go home to the house
I've been away from for so long.

09:27.890 --> 09:30.060
I even have my key, and everything.

09:35.900 --> 09:39.900
I want to return home to my house!

09:57.920 --> 09:59.840
So...

09:59.920 --> 10:03.680
...we are here at that girl's request.

10:03.760 --> 10:05.680
Wow, what a big mansion!

10:05.760 --> 10:08.640
It sure is. It's quite handsome
in its construction, isn't it?

10:08.720 --> 10:10.810
I'd say it's more ominous than handsome.

10:10.890 --> 10:13.810
Anyhow, there's something I'd like to ask you...

10:13.890 --> 10:15.850
What is <i>he</i> doing here?

10:18.900 --> 10:20.230
Yo.

10:20.320 --> 10:23.240
Oh, do you wish it was just the two of us?

10:23.320 --> 10:26.280
That's not what I meant!

10:27.740 --> 10:30.240
If you're inviting others along,
you could've called Himawari-<i>chan</i>...

10:30.330 --> 10:33.830
I should remind you that the young
lady asked <i>you</i> to begin with,

10:33.910 --> 10:36.460
and you directed her to me.

10:36.540 --> 10:38.880
Are you sure that you're not the one
who should be solving this case?

10:38.960 --> 10:40.840
Well then, Yuko-<i>san</i>, why are you...

10:40.920 --> 10:43.260
I just came along because I was invited.

10:43.340 --> 10:44.840
I asked Domeki-<i>kun</i> along for you...

10:44.930 --> 10:48.260
...because I thought you would
be lonesome all by yourself.

10:48.350 --> 10:50.260
To compensate Domeki-<i>kun</i> for his help,

10:50.350 --> 10:54.020
I worked out a deal with him for you to
make bento lunches for him for a month.

10:54.100 --> 10:55.440
Somen noodles will be fine.

10:55.520 --> 10:58.650
Don't go making deals for me
to work without asking me!

10:58.730 --> 11:00.650
And bento lunches are out of the question.

11:00.730 --> 11:03.490
Well, we'll see in due time.

11:11.910 --> 11:12.700
Huh?

11:12.740 --> 11:13.660
What's wrong?

11:13.750 --> 11:18.460
It's just that our client for this job said
that she couldn't go inside her own house.

11:18.540 --> 11:19.670
We're going in, aren't we?

11:19.750 --> 11:22.670
That's what's so strange!
We didn't even use the key!

11:22.750 --> 11:26.840
That probably means that this house
does not recognize our client as its owner.

11:26.930 --> 11:29.260
It looks like we're okay, though.

11:29.340 --> 11:30.720
Just a minute!

12:00.330 --> 12:05.300
"Thank you for coming. Please
proceed straight down this hallway."

12:06.760 --> 12:10.260
So we should go straight, right?
Forgive the intrusion!

12:10.340 --> 12:11.890
Just a minute, please!

12:12.930 --> 12:16.640
Why are you reacting so normally?
Clearly, this is strange, isn't it?

12:16.730 --> 12:18.810
For one thing, why wasn't anyone there?

12:18.890 --> 12:19.810
They're probably busy, you know.

12:19.900 --> 12:23.820
They're busy? You mean, despite having
enough time to write out invitations?

12:23.900 --> 12:26.650
I'm sure they must just like writing letters.

12:26.740 --> 12:27.820
Yuko-<i>san</i>...

12:27.900 --> 12:29.820
Domeki, say something to her.

12:29.910 --> 12:31.820
You'll go bald from worrying so much.

12:31.910 --> 12:33.870
Who are you calling bald?!

12:37.750 --> 12:39.710
"Please open this door."

12:44.340 --> 12:45.670
A wall?

12:45.750 --> 12:47.670
We can't go any farther like this.

12:47.760 --> 12:49.680
Watanuki, you try opening it.

12:49.760 --> 12:50.880
Who, me?

13:00.310 --> 13:03.230
It was chilling to think he would try
to pass off such a knockoff piece on me.

13:03.310 --> 13:05.860
No, I just happened to come across it.

13:08.740 --> 13:10.650
There's definitely something
strange about this house.

13:10.740 --> 13:11.820
What kind of construction is this?

13:11.910 --> 13:15.660
Go and talk with the people who are here now.

13:15.740 --> 13:17.700
Huh? What do you mean?

13:19.330 --> 13:21.830
So that's the sort of
collection you're keeping, huh?

13:21.920 --> 13:25.250
I might have known you'd see
things through different eyes.

13:25.340 --> 13:29.840
Oh, not at all. It's just not the
sort of thing I show off to others.

13:29.920 --> 13:32.840
Ah, we have someone else joining us, do we?

13:32.930 --> 13:36.930
I haven't seen your face around
in our circles. Who might you be?

13:37.930 --> 13:39.520
Ichihara Yuko.

13:40.730 --> 13:42.690
Of course, that's an alias.

13:44.730 --> 13:46.650
Aren't you an interesting lady!

13:46.730 --> 13:49.690
So, ma'am, what do you collect?

13:51.900 --> 13:55.820
Look, if you're collecting something,
you must have a collection, right?

13:55.910 --> 14:01.290
All the other folks here are pretty
famous collectors within our circle.

14:02.330 --> 14:05.670
We're all here in this mansion because it
says there's something hard to find here.

14:05.750 --> 14:06.670
See?

14:06.750 --> 14:11.260
"Your collection is incomplete. If your
goal is to complete your collection,

14:11.340 --> 14:14.090
then by all means, come to my mansion."

14:15.760 --> 14:19.680
Anyone would get upset when they are
told that their collection is incomplete.

14:19.770 --> 14:24.640
Then again, if it really means that
my collection will be completed,

14:24.730 --> 14:26.650
then it will be worth it to have come here.

14:26.730 --> 14:28.860
What is it that you collect, ma'am?

14:31.740 --> 14:32.690
Um...

14:35.320 --> 14:36.660
Mokona!

14:36.740 --> 14:38.870
You idiot! Stay inside there!

14:41.910 --> 14:44.500
Yuko-<i>san</i>'s collection consists of stuffed animals.

14:48.340 --> 14:50.840
How unbelievably common!

14:50.920 --> 14:54.670
It's collecting something that others
don't that makes one a collector.

14:54.760 --> 14:56.720
What about you there, son?

14:57.930 --> 14:59.300
Stamps.

15:00.930 --> 15:02.810
There couldn't be anything more ordinary!

15:02.890 --> 15:04.270
So, how about you?

15:05.310 --> 15:06.690
Let's see...

15:09.310 --> 15:10.690
Supermarket points.

15:12.320 --> 15:13.820
<i>That's</i> your collection?!

15:13.900 --> 15:15.860
Hey, who invited this guy?!

15:27.920 --> 15:29.880
A party at the mansion, or something?

15:30.920 --> 15:32.710
Looks like they're having fun.

15:42.350 --> 15:46.810
So, how do you suppose the owner
of this mansion knew who we were?

15:46.890 --> 15:51.820
Has anyone here ever met
the owner of the mansion?

15:51.900 --> 15:53.280
Unfortunately, no.

15:54.730 --> 15:55.860
How about you?

15:58.740 --> 16:00.820
This really is strange.

16:00.910 --> 16:04.870
If you ask me, your behavior is far stranger,

16:04.950 --> 16:08.670
all gathering here like
this over a single invitation.

16:08.750 --> 16:11.670
You're here too, aren't you?

16:11.750 --> 16:13.670
Don't group me in with you guys!

16:13.750 --> 16:18.680
That miserable mansion owner...
Knock my collection, will he?

16:18.760 --> 16:21.720
Incomplete, is it? Come off it.

16:23.760 --> 16:25.640
Pay him no mind.

16:25.720 --> 16:29.810
You know, everyone here at this
table is an outstanding collector.

16:29.900 --> 16:33.820
I am nearly breathless in admiration.

16:33.900 --> 16:35.650
What are you talking about?

16:35.730 --> 16:37.240
Such modesty, from someone so young.

16:37.320 --> 16:40.240
I'm just speaking the truth.

16:40.320 --> 16:42.820
- We could say the same for you.
- No, no, not at all.

16:42.910 --> 16:43.830
There you go again.

16:43.910 --> 16:45.830
- Indeed.
- Listen to all of you...

16:45.910 --> 16:48.460
I hate to blow my own horn, but...

16:48.540 --> 16:51.080
Naturally, my own tastes are above...

16:57.340 --> 16:59.670
What is that smell?

16:59.760 --> 17:02.680
You're seeing something again, aren't you?

17:02.760 --> 17:05.850
Uh-huh. It's like some kind
of haze. What could it be?

17:05.930 --> 17:09.230
The pride, vanity, and envy the
collectors have amongst each other.

17:09.310 --> 17:12.850
All of it must be swirling
around in here, within this room.

17:22.320 --> 17:23.820
What's the matter?

17:23.910 --> 17:25.830
You're not being affected?!

17:25.910 --> 17:28.080
It's no use! I can't take it anymore!

17:29.150 --> 17:31.110
"Restroom"

18:06.740 --> 18:07.870
This can't be right.

18:10.310 --> 18:12.270
"The restroom is under the stairs"

18:41.320 --> 18:44.280
Why do I have to go to all this trouble?

20:48.900 --> 20:51.280
I'm being watched? But why?

21:10.340 --> 21:13.890
5... 6... 7... 8...

21:14.930 --> 21:16.890
What was I doing again?

21:17.930 --> 21:19.310
Oh, right.

21:37.910 --> 21:40.660
"Dinner has been made
ready in the dining room.

21:40.750 --> 21:43.290
The others have already been led there."

21:46.750 --> 21:49.510
Someone's watching me, all right...

22:05.900 --> 22:06.860
Who's there?

22:51.530 --> 22:54.280
Watanuki, hurry and come sit down.

22:56.910 --> 22:59.660
This mansion really is weird!

22:59.740 --> 23:02.290
You don't say. Never mind that, this is delicious.

23:03.330 --> 23:04.830
Now, hold on a minute.

23:04.910 --> 23:08.250
Who was it that prepared this food?
Don't you find it strange?

23:08.330 --> 23:09.840
You're such a worrywart.

23:09.920 --> 23:12.300
If you don't want it,
you don't have to eat it.

23:30.730 --> 23:35.240
Tell me something, when is our
all-important host going to show himself?

23:35.320 --> 23:39.240
Come to mention it, has anyone ever heard
stories about a mysterious auctioneer,

23:39.320 --> 23:42.830
who holds secret auctions
for preeminent collectors?

23:42.910 --> 23:45.830
It is a famous legend,
according to some sources.

23:45.910 --> 23:49.830
So are you trying to say that
this mansion is an auction house?

23:49.920 --> 23:52.250
Which means that right now,
while we're sitting here,

23:52.340 --> 23:55.300
our host could be watching us somewhere.

23:57.760 --> 24:00.890
I guess he's saying to leave
the room, and to come this way.

24:01.930 --> 24:03.850
Watanuki, let's go.

24:03.930 --> 24:04.890
Okay.

24:13.900 --> 24:15.690
Watanuki, notice anything?

24:18.740 --> 24:20.240
Huh? We're one short!

24:20.320 --> 24:22.240
Yeah, that white-haired gentleman.

24:22.330 --> 24:24.830
Maybe he got lost on the way in here.

24:24.910 --> 24:26.700
I'll go have a look.

24:28.920 --> 24:33.290
I, uh, seem to have had too much to
drink. I'm going to the restroom.

24:41.340 --> 24:43.680
Nobody has returned, huh?

24:43.760 --> 24:47.680
I wonder where our host
is peeking in on us from.

24:47.770 --> 24:50.810
There's probably a spy among us.

24:50.900 --> 24:52.230
What do you mean by that?

24:52.310 --> 24:55.650
I mean you. You've been
pretty relaxed for a while now.

24:55.730 --> 24:56.650
What are you getting at, you--!

24:56.730 --> 25:00.240
Hang on, this is no time to
be fighting among ourselves!

25:00.320 --> 25:02.280
What did you say, coupon bastard?

25:02.370 --> 25:04.830
Isn't having a kid like you
here strange all by itself?

25:04.910 --> 25:05.830
How can you say that?

25:05.910 --> 25:08.290
The lady there is fishy, as well.

25:09.750 --> 25:12.250
Have you two noticed it yet?

25:12.330 --> 25:13.880
We've lost another one.

25:14.920 --> 25:15.710
Huh?!

25:15.750 --> 25:17.880
The old lady is gone!

25:22.760 --> 25:25.850
"Rooms have been
prepared for you to stay over.

25:25.930 --> 25:29.850
Please do not leave your rooms
for any reason during the night."

25:29.930 --> 25:33.310
What is this?! Aren't we
having the auction tonight?!

25:36.320 --> 25:38.650
Yuko-<i>san</i>, what do we do?

25:38.730 --> 25:41.280
They say we have to spend the night,
so we have to spend the night.

25:42.320 --> 25:44.030
You go on ahead to bed.

25:44.120 --> 25:47.700
Something is sure to happen, so watch yourself.

25:48.740 --> 25:51.290
I'm going to stay here a little while longer.

25:55.330 --> 25:57.710
We're having another hard time
just getting to our bedrooms, huh?

25:58.750 --> 26:02.680
There are houses that are a
lot like this one in America.

26:02.760 --> 26:05.680
I've heard that spirits haunt
the homes of multimillionaires,

26:05.760 --> 26:11.270
and so the owners keep building onto
them, in order to confuse the ghosts.

26:11.350 --> 26:13.730
This place could be the same way.

26:14.730 --> 26:18.480
S-Stop talking like that!
How about something more pleasant--?

26:19.730 --> 26:21.490
Don't leave me behind!

26:22.740 --> 26:23.700
Is this it?

26:26.320 --> 26:28.060
"Please pull the door"

26:32.750 --> 26:33.710
That's strange...

26:38.750 --> 26:39.300
Hey.

26:39.340 --> 26:40.300
What?!

26:42.030 --> 26:44.490
"Please pull the door to the right"

26:44.340 --> 26:47.300
To the right?! That was misleading!

26:54.310 --> 26:56.440
I've got to ask, why am I the only one...

26:56.520 --> 26:58.810
who has to stay in a double room, with you?

26:58.900 --> 27:01.230
Then again, I'd be a little uncomfortable by myself--

27:01.320 --> 27:03.240
No, make that <i>very</i> uncomfortable.

27:03.320 --> 27:05.860
Besides, which room is Yuko-<i>san</i> in?

27:07.740 --> 27:09.660
I wonder if she's okay all alone.

27:09.740 --> 27:14.250
Maybe we should be more
worried about ourselves, though.

27:14.330 --> 27:16.290
Domeki, in case anything happens...

27:17.750 --> 27:19.670
Listen, you!

27:19.750 --> 27:21.250
Of all the...

27:21.340 --> 27:22.710
I'm going to bed!

27:31.350 --> 27:35.690
Looks like we've gotten into
something pretty wild here.

27:35.770 --> 27:38.730
I wonder if we're going to
safely make it till morning.

27:49.910 --> 27:53.490
"You are safe here.
Please have a good night's sleep"

27:54.910 --> 27:56.660
What does this mean?

27:56.750 --> 27:57.670
Haven't you gone to sleep yet?

27:57.750 --> 27:58.870
I'm going, already!

28:05.920 --> 28:07.840
Ready yet?

28:07.930 --> 28:10.260
Not yet.

28:10.340 --> 28:12.680
Ready yet?

28:12.760 --> 28:14.680
Not yet.

28:14.770 --> 28:16.680
Ready yet?

28:16.770 --> 28:18.730
Ready.

28:53.760 --> 28:54.890
You found me!

28:56.350 --> 28:58.890
These? These are my new beanbags.

28:58.980 --> 29:00.940
I've already collected this many.

29:02.310 --> 29:06.230
Why don't you collect something too, like I do?

29:06.320 --> 29:09.860
It may as well be something
that no one else would collect.

29:09.950 --> 29:11.860
Say, for example...

29:27.760 --> 29:29.260
Domeki!

29:29.340 --> 29:31.880
Hey, Domeki!

29:33.930 --> 29:35.300
What happened?

29:39.350 --> 29:42.230
"You are safe." The writing has changed!

29:42.310 --> 29:46.690
Before, it said "You are safe here."
So what about Domeki and Yuko-<i>san</i>...

30:04.750 --> 30:06.920
The letter said we weren't
supposed to leave our rooms.

30:09.340 --> 30:11.720
Come on, you're a man, aren't you, Watanuki?!

31:15.740 --> 31:19.200
Domeki! Yuko-<i>san</i>!

31:23.330 --> 31:24.870
Is the sound coming from here?

31:31.340 --> 31:32.710
No, it isn't.

31:47.350 --> 31:48.730
From in here?

32:06.910 --> 32:08.710
Butterfly specimens?

32:10.330 --> 32:12.880
But these are just the antennae...

32:36.530 --> 32:38.820
Oh, it's you, Watanuki.

32:38.900 --> 32:41.030
Don't you "Oh, it's you" me!

32:41.120 --> 32:43.830
I was looking for you and Yuko-<i>san</i>!

32:43.910 --> 32:45.830
You were worried about us?

32:45.910 --> 32:49.670
It's not that. Before I knew it, you were gone.

32:49.750 --> 32:51.670
The room had changed, too.

32:51.750 --> 32:55.250
So I started walking around
the house, and ended up here.

32:55.340 --> 32:59.880
Me too. But I get the feeling that we were led here.

33:26.740 --> 33:27.830
Fences?

33:27.910 --> 33:30.040
Barbed wire barricades, probably.

33:30.120 --> 33:32.250
A barbed wire barricade collection room?

33:32.330 --> 33:35.840
And a butterfly antenna collection room before that.

33:35.920 --> 33:37.300
What's next?

33:48.350 --> 33:49.730
Collars?

34:53.330 --> 34:54.710
Spoons?

35:02.760 --> 35:03.840
Huh?

35:03.920 --> 35:05.510
This one...

35:07.760 --> 35:09.930
...was from dinner earlier...

35:11.350 --> 35:12.730
Watanuki!

35:20.730 --> 35:22.650
Isn't that...

35:22.740 --> 35:25.650
...the man who disappeared after dinner?

35:25.740 --> 35:28.820
Why is there a picture of him here?

35:28.910 --> 35:31.830
Oh, you boys are awake too, huh?

35:31.910 --> 35:34.250
Who can sleep at a time like this?

35:34.330 --> 35:38.880
Ha! You were just trying to get the jump
on us to endear yourself to our host.

35:40.750 --> 35:41.840
I dare you to say that again!

35:41.920 --> 35:43.840
I could say the same about you!

35:43.920 --> 35:46.470
Don't get so worked up just because I
hit the nail on the head, you geezer!

35:46.550 --> 35:51.680
Please don't quarrel at a time like this.
We might not be able to get out of here.

35:51.760 --> 35:54.270
So what?

35:54.350 --> 35:58.270
I want to complete my collection, no matter what.

35:58.350 --> 36:00.900
I won't be outdone, either!

36:05.320 --> 36:06.820
This is too weird.

36:06.900 --> 36:09.820
In here, <i>we</i> might be the weird ones.

36:09.910 --> 36:13.290
Let's go. Whatever the case,
let's find Yuko-<i>san</i> and the exit.

36:48.740 --> 36:49.660
Out of my way!

36:49.740 --> 36:52.240
Those say where the collections are!

36:52.320 --> 36:56.290
"You broke your promise
not to leave your rooms."

36:57.330 --> 37:00.670
"As punishment, you will
have to participate in my game."

37:00.750 --> 37:05.250
"Hide-and-seek. If you can find
me within ten minutes, you win."

37:05.340 --> 37:06.880
"If you do not find me, you lose.

37:06.960 --> 37:08.260
If you win, I will give you what you desire,

37:08.340 --> 37:09.880
and if you lose, you will play a penalty game.

37:09.970 --> 37:11.840
Now, let the games begin."

37:11.930 --> 37:13.300
What is this?!

37:20.940 --> 37:24.310
He's messing with us!
Hey, come on out, already!

37:27.320 --> 37:28.650
The ceiling!

37:28.740 --> 37:32.660
What is this?! What do we do?!

37:32.740 --> 37:34.240
There it is, there it is, the exit!

37:34.320 --> 37:35.240
Move it, geezer!

37:35.330 --> 37:36.830
What are you doing, you punk?!

37:36.910 --> 37:38.290
Watanuki!

37:40.750 --> 37:42.080
This pattern...

37:43.540 --> 37:44.840
It's the same as the one I saw in my dream!

37:44.920 --> 37:47.840
That's it! Yuko-<i>san</i>'s key! If only we had it...

37:47.920 --> 37:49.880
But that would be too convenient...

37:49.970 --> 37:51.090
Here it is.

37:54.760 --> 37:56.680
Could Yuko-<i>san</i> have known that this would happen?

37:56.760 --> 37:57.890
- It won't open!
- Give it here.

38:03.940 --> 38:05.520
All right, hurry!

38:15.740 --> 38:17.870
This place showed up in my dream, too.

38:21.330 --> 38:24.290
Looks like this place hasn't
been opened in decades.

38:31.920 --> 38:33.680
That girl!

38:33.760 --> 38:35.300
You know her?

38:37.350 --> 38:41.890
That girl has to be the one who
locked us up inside this mansion.

38:41.980 --> 38:43.690
Hurry, we don't have much time.

38:43.770 --> 38:46.270
We have to find her, and
get Yuko-<i>san</i> back from her.

38:46.360 --> 38:48.900
Then we'll have nothing
more to do with this mansion.

38:50.730 --> 38:52.240
How many more minutes do we have?

38:52.320 --> 38:54.820
I don't know.

38:53.180 --> 38:54.470
"4 minutes left"

38:54.910 --> 38:58.280
Damn it, she's toying with us!
We'll find her, that's for sure!

39:03.150 --> 39:04.320
"3 minutes left"

39:04.750 --> 39:06.670
Are we running somewhere in particular?

39:06.750 --> 39:07.670
Nope!

39:07.750 --> 39:10.460
But right now, we've got
no choice but to search!

39:09.490 --> 39:13.490
"2 minutes left"

39:10.550 --> 39:11.920
Oh, no!

39:13.340 --> 39:14.930
Dead end.

39:25.770 --> 39:26.850
This is strange.

39:26.940 --> 39:28.900
The arrangement of the rooms is different.

39:31.900 --> 39:33.690
We're right back where we started!

39:34.900 --> 39:35.820
Huh?

39:35.900 --> 39:37.700
What do we do now?

39:37.530 --> 39:43.520
"1 minute left"

39:43.750 --> 39:45.080
Damn it!

39:51.750 --> 39:53.300
Watanuki, what's wrong?

40:23.910 --> 40:25.830
You found me.

40:25.910 --> 40:27.660
Who are you?!

40:27.750 --> 40:29.250
Who are you talking to?

40:29.330 --> 40:32.670
I see, if I'm the only one who can
see you, then that means you're...

40:32.750 --> 40:37.840
People come to possess a number
of things during their short lives.

40:37.920 --> 40:41.850
Among them are those people who
insist on owning certain specific items.

40:41.930 --> 40:45.270
You mean those people we call collectors, right?

40:45.350 --> 40:47.890
Yuko-<i>san</i>! Thank goodness!

40:48.940 --> 40:52.810
No sooner did your presence
disappear than here you are again...

40:52.900 --> 40:55.320
Watanuki here is strongly sensitive to spirits,

40:55.400 --> 40:57.820
and the spooks can't come near Domeki.

40:57.900 --> 41:01.820
With the two of them paired together,
they make for a good blinder, don't they?

41:01.910 --> 41:03.660
So that's it.

41:03.740 --> 41:06.910
Now, what sort of penalty
game are you going to put us to?

41:07.330 --> 41:12.920
Let me show you my collection,
which I have never shown to anyone else.

41:16.920 --> 41:19.260
What is this?

41:19.340 --> 41:24.680
My auction resulted in only the
spoon collector being placed in here.

41:24.760 --> 41:26.260
Auction?

41:26.350 --> 41:30.850
The auction I held to choose who
among you would enter my collection.

41:30.940 --> 41:34.020
Each of the collectors that
gathered at your mansion...

41:34.110 --> 41:36.820
...were to be items in your collection.

41:36.900 --> 41:43.240
I auctioned them off in my mind, to see
who was worthy of my grand collection.

41:43.320 --> 41:45.830
What happened to the ones you didn't choose?!

41:45.910 --> 41:50.660
Unfortunately, those who were not
chosen were all placed within a picture.

41:50.750 --> 41:53.250
By any chance, do you mean
that picture in the drawing room?

41:53.330 --> 41:56.290
There were six individuals
that joined them tonight.

41:57.340 --> 42:02.260
Collectors have an unusual sense of
attachment to some specific thing.

42:02.340 --> 42:05.850
We call them by the generic name "-holic."

42:05.930 --> 42:10.850
But what if those objects weren't "things,"
but souls, instead?

42:10.930 --> 42:13.850
What you have here is a collection of collectors.

42:13.940 --> 42:15.860
What you wanted to collect were the spirits...

42:15.940 --> 42:20.240
...of those whose hearts were captivated by "things."

42:20.320 --> 42:25.240
Now that you have collected
this many souls, are you satisfied?

42:25.320 --> 42:27.280
I still haven't collected it.

42:28.330 --> 42:31.830
I still haven't collected what I really want.

42:31.910 --> 42:35.830
But I'm sure that if I had your soul...

42:35.920 --> 42:38.670
It's nice that you'd think so much of me,

42:38.750 --> 42:42.670
but unfortunately, I don't collect anything.

42:42.760 --> 42:44.890
Still, you have the power to collect,

42:44.970 --> 42:47.850
however unintentionally, the souls of others.

42:47.930 --> 42:50.680
If that doesn't make you the ultimate collector,

42:50.770 --> 42:52.270
then what else would you call it?

42:52.350 --> 42:56.860
You'll forgive me, but I'm not about to
let myself be trapped inside this mansion.

42:56.940 --> 42:59.230
Besides...

42:59.320 --> 43:01.280
...<i>you're</i> the one who is caught here.

43:31.930 --> 43:33.890
Domeki, we have to protect Yuko-<i>san</i>!

44:37.910 --> 44:39.830
Stop it!

44:39.920 --> 44:41.880
What are you doing?! Let me go!

44:41.960 --> 44:43.880
Let me go! Stop!

44:45.760 --> 44:47.260
Don't!

44:47.340 --> 44:49.260
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

44:49.340 --> 44:50.720
No!

45:34.760 --> 45:35.720
Take this!

45:39.350 --> 45:41.310
Watanuki! Heads up!

45:52.910 --> 45:57.660
You are the spirit that
possesses this mansion.

45:57.740 --> 46:01.670
You've stored up this much
power over the last hundred years.

46:01.750 --> 46:04.830
No matter how many people's souls you collect,

46:04.920 --> 46:07.670
no matter if you were to
add me to your collection,

46:07.750 --> 46:10.840
there is no way you can be content.

46:10.920 --> 46:12.300
I feel sorry for you.

46:43.920 --> 46:45.880
This game ends now!

46:55.760 --> 46:57.100
You fell for it.

47:04.770 --> 47:05.940
Yuko-<i>san</i>!

47:08.940 --> 47:11.820
I've finally gotten you.

47:11.900 --> 47:15.820
Will my heart be satisfied now?

47:15.910 --> 47:18.280
Why, you! Give Yuko-<i>san</i> back!

47:19.330 --> 47:22.870
I'll have to dispose of you two, as well.

47:28.130 --> 47:29.880
I've finally found it.

47:33.920 --> 47:37.680
It was necessary to get inside your mind...

47:37.760 --> 47:40.890
...in order for me to obtain what Watanuki found.

47:44.350 --> 47:46.270
Remember.

47:46.350 --> 47:49.270
This is what is important to you.

47:49.360 --> 47:52.320
This is what you truly want.

48:49.750 --> 48:50.880
The mansion--!

49:00.760 --> 49:03.100
Yuko-<i>san</i>! You're safe!

49:04.350 --> 49:07.270
Huh? Who is this old lady?

49:07.350 --> 49:12.690
Thank you for granting my wish.

49:12.770 --> 49:15.820
He's still all withdrawn inside his own shell.

49:15.900 --> 49:18.280
You're the one who will have to use this.

49:23.740 --> 49:26.870
I'm sure I can make do without it.

49:32.330 --> 49:36.300
Do you remember... who I am?

49:59.740 --> 50:01.820
Please don't cry, now.

50:01.910 --> 50:05.280
You are moving away, so there's
nothing we can do about it.

50:06.740 --> 50:08.660
Here, you forgot this.

50:08.750 --> 50:10.710
This was important to you, right?

50:18.920 --> 50:21.260
When I get bigger,

50:21.340 --> 50:25.300
I'm going to make sure
I come back to this house someday,

50:26.350 --> 50:29.720
so watch over the house
for me until then, okay?

50:31.770 --> 50:34.270
All right.

50:34.350 --> 50:36.270
Promise me.

50:36.360 --> 50:37.860
I promise.

50:37.940 --> 50:40.820
Until then, I'm going to collect a whole lot

50:40.900 --> 50:45.820
of something special for you.
Something you'll be proud of.

50:45.910 --> 50:49.040
Something that nobody else would collect.

50:49.120 --> 50:55.880
Pinky promise! Swallow a
thousand needles if I'm lying!

50:59.750 --> 51:00.840
I've missed you.

51:00.920 --> 51:05.680
I'm sorry for keeping you so
lonely for such a long time.

51:05.760 --> 51:07.850
I went and bought back the house,

51:07.930 --> 51:10.720
but the key didn't work, and I couldn't come in.

51:11.770 --> 51:13.890
Before I knew what I was doing,

51:13.980 --> 51:17.860
I had forgotten the reason
why I was keeping my collection,

51:17.940 --> 51:20.690
despite having started it because
I really wanted you to see it,

51:20.780 --> 51:23.240
and tell me how good it was.

51:23.320 --> 51:27.820
Please, stop doing it now, okay?

51:27.910 --> 51:28.830
Okay.

51:28.910 --> 51:31.830
Still, I'm so glad you remember me.

51:31.910 --> 51:38.250
So much time has passed,
and I have gotten so very old.

51:38.330 --> 51:41.250
You haven't changed at all.

51:41.340 --> 51:43.880
You're just as you were long ago, when you left.

51:47.340 --> 51:48.890
I'm home.

51:50.760 --> 51:52.310
Welcome back.

51:53.350 --> 51:55.690
We'll be together from now on, right?

51:55.770 --> 51:58.310
Yes, together from now on.

52:31.350 --> 52:32.930
I'm lightheaded...

52:38.940 --> 52:42.860
What do you suppose will
become of that mansion now?

52:42.940 --> 52:46.240
The old lady has decided to
have it turned into a museum.

52:46.320 --> 52:48.240
She's going to be its curator.

52:48.320 --> 52:50.240
Will she be able to handle that by herself?

52:50.320 --> 52:51.820
Not to worry.

52:51.910 --> 52:54.830
The collectors that were freed
said that they would help her.

52:54.910 --> 52:57.830
So it won't be a closed-up
mansion anymore, huh?

52:57.910 --> 53:00.250
Still, I had no idea that
the girl at the mansion...

53:00.330 --> 53:02.040
...and the young lady
who came to your house,

53:02.130 --> 53:05.250
were spirit projections of that old lady.

53:05.340 --> 53:09.720
When she came to the house, I thought
about turning her down for a moment.

53:10.930 --> 53:14.310
For some reason, as I listened to
her, I started sympathizing with her.

53:16.930 --> 53:19.850
Yuko-<i>san</i>, have you had
some sort of painful past love,

53:19.940 --> 53:22.310
or are you lovesick
over someone, or something?

53:23.360 --> 53:24.730
Would you like to know?

53:27.740 --> 53:29.650
I'm getting an emergency message from Syaoran!

53:29.740 --> 53:31.660
From those kids?

53:31.740 --> 53:34.660
Yuko-<i>san</i>! I need to save the Land of Birds!

53:34.740 --> 53:38.660
I need to open a magic birdcage
in order to save the Land of Birds!

53:38.750 --> 53:41.250
In other words, you need a key, right?

53:41.330 --> 53:44.250
I have just the thing.

53:44.340 --> 53:48.840
A key that takes in the user's
wishes, and opens everything.

53:48.920 --> 53:50.260
Thank you so much.

53:50.340 --> 53:53.680
However, I will need to be compensated first.

53:53.760 --> 53:56.260
Is there anything I can give you...

53:56.350 --> 53:58.720
Um, how about this?

53:59.930 --> 54:02.850
That bell is a symbol of the bond

54:02.940 --> 54:05.860
between you and something dear to you, isn't it?

54:05.940 --> 54:08.530
Very well. Mokona?

54:12.740 --> 54:14.870
Okay then, good luck.

54:17.910 --> 54:20.660
This is a real treasure, isn't it?

54:20.750 --> 54:23.290
Maybe I'll use it the next time
I need to call you, Watanuki.

54:25.750 --> 54:27.920
Domeki, you were in the bath a long time.

54:32.340 --> 54:33.840
Himawari-<i>chan</i>!

54:33.930 --> 54:36.680
Hello, Watanuki-<i>kun</i>.

54:36.760 --> 54:38.890
Wow, what a pretty view!

54:40.930 --> 54:43.850
Yuko-<i>san</i>, thanks for inviting me over.

54:43.940 --> 54:48.520
Sure thing, Himawari-<i>chan</i>.
Watanuki wanted me to invite you over.

54:51.900 --> 54:56.820
Yuko-<i>san</i>, for the first time in my life,
I am sincerely grateful to you!

54:56.910 --> 54:58.240
Well then...

54:58.330 --> 55:00.660
...now that the work is done,
how about some of this?

55:00.750 --> 55:03.870
Ah, that was in the room
that hadn't been opened.

55:05.750 --> 55:09.250
This is my compensation for
granting the old lady's wish.

55:09.340 --> 55:12.050
And, my compensation
for granting your wish...

55:12.130 --> 55:15.300
...to invite Himawari-<i>chan</i> over will be...

55:17.350 --> 55:18.720
What is it?

55:20.350 --> 55:22.850
I've finally gotten my sake.

55:22.930 --> 55:24.850
Take care of the snacks.

55:24.940 --> 55:26.270
Huh? Why me?

55:26.350 --> 55:28.860
Because your cooking is so good, Watanuki-<i>kun</i>!

55:28.940 --> 55:32.820
All right, for you, Himawari-<i>chan</i>, I'll do my best!

55:32.900 --> 55:34.820
A sashimi platter would be nice.

55:34.900 --> 55:36.820
Who asked you what you liked?!

55:36.910 --> 55:38.660
I want sashimi, too!

55:38.740 --> 55:40.240
Okay, I'm on it!

55:40.330 --> 55:41.660
Don't forget the wasabi.

55:41.740 --> 55:44.250
And why should I be taking orders from you?!

55:44.330 --> 55:47.290
- If that's okay...
- Mm-hmm, I'll take care of it!

55:50.920 --> 55:54.130
Here's to a wonderful picture.

56:10.940 --> 56:20.940
<i>I didn't mind the shiver I got from</i>
<i>those callous fingers of yours,</i>

56:21.120 --> 56:30.880
<i>as though you were clinging directly</i>
<i>to a thin membrane around my body.</i>

56:30.960 --> 56:40.850
<i>But the thing about you is that</i>
<i>you always lie if left to yourself.</i>

56:40.930 --> 56:50.270
<i>You figured me for a fool</i>
<i>right from the start.</i>

56:50.350 --> 57:00.030
<i>I never thought a day like</i>
<i>this would ever come.</i>

57:00.110 --> 57:10.110
<i>I can even feel your</i>
<i>presence there still.</i>

57:14.130 --> 57:23.850
<i>Ever since you left, my body has</i>
<i>been dried up and chrysalis-colored.</i>

57:23.930 --> 57:29.060
<i>I'm being reborn here</i>
<i>in this cold, wintry room,</i>

57:29.140 --> 57:33.860
<i>as though I were a beautiful butterfly.</i>

57:33.940 --> 57:43.820
<i>Little by little,</i>
<i>I open my still-damp wings,</i>

57:43.910 --> 57:53.250
<i>so as to not let anyone ruin them,</i>
<i>and dream about flying through the sky.</i>

57:53.330 --> 58:03.260
<i>If that day were</i>
<i>to suddenly come upon me,</i>

58:03.340 --> 58:13.340
<i>I wonder where I should fly</i>
<i>away to with these wings.</i>

58:34.750 --> 58:44.680
<i>I am going to forget your name, as though</i>
<i>you were livestock that had no name.</i>

58:44.760 --> 58:53.850
<i>I would rather wipe you out</i>
<i>entirely than remember you and weep.</i>

58:53.940 --> 59:03.820
<i>Will that day ever come along?</i>

59:03.900 --> 59:13.830
<i>Will I ever be allowed</i>
<i>any days with you again?</i>

59:13.910 --> 59:23.910
<i>Will that day ever come along?</i>

59:24.130 --> 59:33.730
<i>When will that wonderful day be?</i>
